# .npmrc — authentication and scope-to-registry mapping for GitHub Packages
#
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT:
#   1. Copy to .npmrc (which is gitignored — never commit tokens):
#        cp .github/npmrc-github-packages .npmrc
#   2. Replace ${GITHUB_TOKEN} with a GitHub personal access token (PAT)
#      that has read:packages scope:
#        https://github.com/settings/tokens
#   3. npm install @bandersnatch0x/amber-protocol
#
# CI (GitHub Actions):
#   The publish workflow (publish-github-packages.yml) builds this
#   configuration on the fly using secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN — no setup needed.
#
# NPM packages with the @bandersnatch0x scope are resolved from GitHub
# Packages instead of the default npm registry. All other packages
# continue to use the npm registry.

@bandersnatch0x:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${GITHUB_TOKEN}
